                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "For less than 2GB, you'll get a very simple looking ARPG at first glance but a very deep and satisfying game that doesn't beat around the bush.\nYou launch the game, you are instantly in a hub with all the vendors and crafters available from the get go, with portals to take you where you will fight monsters.\nIf you have played a lot of Diablo3/4 and Path of Exile 1/2's endgames, Chronicon's ENTIRE GAMEPLAY is that.\n\nA story? Who cares. Even the writers know you don't.\n\nYour characters' appearances won't change based on what they are equipped with.\nInstead, you get skins and dyes unlockable through the completion of content/achievements.\n\nThe gameplay is responsive, maybe a bit clunky with the basic autoattack on the left click, but that can re-mapped/changed in-game.\n\nThe sound design is good, pretty chunky.\n\nThe crafting systems are not necessarily complex but they are very permissive and there are many mechanics to take into account. If you're into optimizing spreadsheets, it is right up your alley.\nAn item you got in very early game interests you for your final build? Keep it, upgrade it along the way and take it to max level. YOU CAN.\nA legendary item has an effect you want for your final build? Keep it until endgame, turn it into a rune and slap it onto your gear. IT'S THAT SIMPLE.\nYou fat-fingered a craft? Do not worry, your item isn't permanently broken. Just transmute it with a stack of keys and you will be able to modify it again.\nYOU CAN MODIFY EVERY PORTION OF YOUR ITEMS HOWEVER AND WHENEVER YOU DESIRE.\nImo Chronicon has the best crafting system out all of ARPGs, period. The close second is Slormancer because they are extremely similar in functions.\n\nLoot is rare, but not exceedingly rare that you would become frustrated trying to find it, and MAGIC FIND exists.\nEach DLC has its own activities and mechanics that grant new ways to customize your gear on top of the rest.\nNot only that, but you will also gain power by simply playing continuously.\nIf you have experienced Diablo3's Paragon system, there is a similar feature here. Time played = XP = More stats\n\nYour 15 minutes sessions will turn into 8 hours without you even realizing it.\nAnd even if you do not have the time, 15 minutes is plenty enough to complete a few endgame activities.\nBecause all specific kinds of loot can be targetted by doing their related activities.\nYou will always be rewarded with something.\n\nThere is no fear of missing out here. No seasons. No forced online mode. No competition.\nYou progress and you learn as you play, pure and simple.\nAn easy 9.5/10 game.",
